Here are three structured development goals based on your notes. They are designed to be professional, ambitious, and aligned with the RTX (Raytheon Technologies) context you described.

I have structured these as: Goal Title, Strategic Description (the "bullet points" regarding what you want to achieve), and Key Milestones (measurable outcomes).

Goal 1: Drive Strategic Growth through Winning CRAD Proposals & Technical Leadership

Description & Strategy:

Build Winning Proposals: Lead the creation of successful research proposals for external entities (CRAD), specifically targeting high-value opportunities.

Align Technical Strategy: Translate complex customer needs into viable research proposals that align strictly with RTX strategic priorities.

Adaptive AI Leadership: Demonstrate agility in proposal writing to address the rapidly changing AI landscape, ensuring our solutions remain on the cutting edge of technology.

Grow Technical Leadership: Expand sphere of influence by leading proposal teams and mentoring junior staff on proposal best practices (building proposals for others).

Key Milestones:

Q1/Q2: Identify and lead the technical volume for at least two major CRAD proposal submissions.

Q3: Secure funding for at least one new project, establishing a pipeline for future work.

Ongoing: Conduct a "lessons learned" or best-practice session for the team on translating customer pain points into funded research.

Ongoing: Achieve a win-rate or customer-feedback score that demonstrates alignment with external customer requirements.

Goal 2: Pioneer Ontology-Driven Enterprise Data Governance

Description & Strategy:

Enterprise Integration: Lead the integration of ontology-based approaches into the wider Data Governance framework to bring enterprise-wide capability.

Network & Influence: Build a strong network of Data Governance stakeholders across Business Units (BUs) to evangelize the value of semantic standards.

Business Value Realization: Clearly communicate the ROI of this approach to leadership, connecting data governance to future business value and data monetization.

Scalable Solutions: Secure funding from BUs to run specific pilot projects, ensuring these projects are "ideal candidates" that can be replicated across the enterprise.

Key Milestones:

Q1: Establish a formal working group or community of practice with Data Governance leads from key BUs.

Q2: Secure BU funding/buy-in for one pilot project demonstrating ontology in data governance.

Q3: Deliver a prototype or proof-of-concept that validates the ontological approach and present the value proposition/ROI to senior leadership.

Q4: Create a "playbook" or roadmap for replicating the successful pilot across other Business Units.

Goal 3: Solidify Industry Authority & Prepare for Technical Fellow Path

Description & Strategy:

Technical Eminence: Solidify role as the key technical leader in AI and Semantics within the organization.

Strategic Collaboration: Deepen collaboration with EDX AI and RTRC AI teams to identify synergies and drive unified technical strategies for the Business Units.

External Influence: Active participation in standard bodies to become the primary point of contact for this domain, effectively influencing industry standards to benefit the organization.

Fellow Roadmap: Systematically prepare for the Fellow application process by identifying gaps and acquiring deeper competence in strategic areas.

Key Milestones:

Q1: Complete a gap analysis against the Technical Fellow requirements and create a closure plan.

Q2: Submit and publish one high-impact research paper in a top-tier conference or journal.

Q3: Join a relevant standard body committee or working group and attend one major industry conference to represent the organization.

Q4: Complete a specific advanced course/certification to acquire deeper competence in an emerging AI/Semantic area (e.g., Neuro-symbolic AI or similar).
